  "body": "### Summary\nAs a SwiftHFR user, I want a list's loading, empty and failure states to be either legacy's or a recorded deliberate difference, so that the parity gate (#693, LOT-164) has no silent UX change.\n\n### Scope\n- Legacy (`87fe0d1c`) shows these states as rows inside the list:\n  - a red « Erreur : … » row;\n  - a « Aucune categorie / Aucun topic / Aucun favori / Aucun message » row;\n  - sources: `MainWindow.swift:160-169`, `:711-719`; `Favorites.swift:682-694`; `MPListView.swift:595-602`.\n- Legacy has no full-screen spinner on lists, only the toolbar icon spinning. Other screens:\n  - profile: « Chargement du profil... » / « Profil indisponible » (`UserProfileView.swift:520-529`, `:569-590`);\n  - reader: « Chargement... » / « Erreur : … » + « Réessayer » (`MessagesView.swift:3358-3370`, `:5199-5207`).\n- SwiftHFR uses:\n  - `ScreenStateView` / `LoadFailureView` full screen;\n  - a `LoadFailureBanner` over kept content;\n  - `EmptyStateView`.\n\n  Sources: `ForumListView.swift:38-56`, `TopicListView.swift:299-315`, `MessageListView.swift:95-146`, `UserProfileView.swift:42`, `:70-72`, `ReaderStatusViews.swift:25-37`. The shared views come from #1306.\n- Catégories has no empty state at all.\n\n### Decision needed\n(a) Keep SwiftHFR's model, record one GAP row (`### Ledger` gap-new, H.1 b), and give Catégories an empty state; or (b) port legacy's inline rows.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The decided model is applied through the shared `ScreenStateView` / `EmptyStateView` only, with tests on `ScreenLoadState`.\n\nFrom the consistency matrix of #693 (PR #1306, w693).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
